&lt;p&gt;These are &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-achievement-badges&quot;&gt;SCP Achievement Badges&lt;/a&gt;, a cool little system made for fun by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1229263&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606853688&quot; alt=&quot;RJB_R&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1229263)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r&quot;  &gt;RJB_R&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;. Yes, I know that technically I don&#039;t count for the &amp;quot;International Skip Of Mystery&amp;quot; mystery achievement, but English isn&#039;t my main language so that sorta counts. For the explanation about the &amp;quot;Certificate Of Attendance&amp;quot;, which requires for me to add to a Collaborative Log, I was the one who created the two reimaginings of two of the &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/roget-s-proposal&quot;&gt;Roget&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/roget-s-conspiracy-theory-for-scp-001&quot;&gt;Proposals&lt;/a&gt; in the &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/abridged-retirement-proposals&quot;&gt;Abridged Retirement Proposals&lt;/a&gt; during its drafting phase, so that also technically counts.&lt;/p&gt;
